docs/DECISIONS.md:2011:- Decided: `POST /ideas` runs that flow inside the service: luna gets the same tools the MCP front offers (search, view, evaluate) plus finish, and a system prompt (`prompts/idea-v4.txt`) that says how to work: break the idea into two to four parts (the thing itself, its drivers, what could break it), search for each part, read what matters, map each part to every view that answers or moves it, evaluate a dollar number, finish with the reading. Code runs the tools, remembers which views the agent has actually seen (a finish may name no other), evaluates the claim itself, and archives every turn so a card replays for $0. The MCP front's instructions carry the same recipe for an external agent. Measured before this change: one call over the top-10 of one search mapped a median of one view per idea (49 probes); the two-step prompt over 20 candidates mapped a median of two.
