EN A ladder has five rungs. Asset theses run from strongly bullish to strongly bearish, describing business impact; theme theses name five ordered outcomes without good/bad labels. Use two rungs for yes/no rather than forcing five: bullish/bearish for assets; named outcomes for themes, such as signed by the deadline/not signed.
224 LADDER_RULES.1 @226
ZH 每一格写成一个能核对的结果：可以是一个数落在哪段区间，也可以是一件事到了哪一步。格和格不重叠、不留空，到期时正好一格成立：涨 50% 及以上、涨 10% 及以上不到 50%、涨跌都不到 10%、降 10% 及以上不到 80%、降 80% 及以上，每个边界只属于一格，到期拿到实际数，一定落进其中一格；写成“涨很多、涨一点”就对不出来。没有含糊的“部分”：部分做到的，写清楚是什么，单独成一格（“发许可，但附条件”）。中性跟什么比，写在那一格的条件里。
EN Each rung is verifiable: a numeric interval or event stage. Rungs must be exhaustive and non-overlapping, so exactly one applies at expiry. For example: up at least 50%; up 10% to under 50%; change under 10% either way; down 10% to under 80%; down at least 80%. Every boundary belongs to one rung. “Up a lot/a little” cannot be checked. Avoid vague partial outcomes; specify the partial state, such as conditional licences, as a distinct rung. State the comparison underlying neutral.
225 LADDER_RULES.2 @227
