EN The replacing evidence, where a speaker revises a statement/number, an official confirms/denies a rumour, or the original source revises/deletes it. Deletion has no replacement evidence. Replaced evidence no longer counts but remains in history.
497 ORDER_RULES.0 @450
ZH 只有信息能产生证据；观点之间只传通知，不传证据，所以观点不会自己证明自己。
EN Only incoming information creates evidence. Theses send notifications, not evidence, so they cannot prove themselves.
498 ORDER_RULES.1 @451
ZH 每条观点只由一个队列来写：主题观点由主题的队列写，对象观点由它所属的公司、加密货币或商品的队列写；写进库时，同一条信息先写主题，再写对象；重判的先后另按依赖排（见“一条信息引起的变化算一轮”那条）。别的队列要它改的（它依赖的观点结论变了、要它重判，或者被替代的证据要连过来），作为通知交给它自己的队列，带着那条信息的顺序号。
EN One queue writes each thesis: the theme's queue for theme theses; the company, cryptocurrency or commodity queue for asset theses. Within an item, write themes before assets. Rejudgement order follows dependencies under the round rule. Other queues send requests, such as dependency changes or replacement links, to the owning queue with the item's sequence number.
499 ORDER_RULES.2 @452
ZH 先后按顺序号排，不用电脑时钟。一条信息只读顺序号比它小的信息写下的内容，加上这一轮里它自己已经写下的；结果要和一条一条按顺序处理完全一样；几条信息同时处理时，一条信息读到的东西（搜出来的清单也算）在它写进库之前被别的信息改了，就重新做一次。
EN Order by sequence, never the computer clock. An item reads only records from earlier sequences plus its own round's writes. The result must match serial processing. If concurrent work changes anything it read, including search lists, before commit, redo the affected work.
500 ORDER_RULES.3 @453
ZH 一条信息引起的变化算一轮：先做完连证据、建观点、接续和连依赖，再按依赖先后重判：先判被依赖的观点，再判依赖它的，后者读的是前者这一轮刚判完的结论（状态和理由）；每条观点这一轮只判一次。美联储这样的观点被很多观点依赖：它判完写“变了”，依赖它的才各判一次；写“没变”，到此为止。
EN One item's changes form a round. Finish evidence links, thesis creation, succession and dependencies, then rejudge in dependency order. Dependants read conclusions freshly judged in that round. Judge each thesis once. A widely depended-on thesis such as the Fed rate triggers each dependant once only if it declares its conclusion changed; otherwise propagation stops.
501 ORDER_RULES.4 @454
ZH 记录只加不改：观点的问题、梯子和到期日写下就不动；比对、重判、接续、关掉、重新打开、标注，都是新加一条记录，带顺序号。
EN Append-only records: questions, ladders and due dates are immutable. Matching, rejudgement, succession, closure, reopening and labels append records with sequence numbers.
502 ORDER_RULES.5 @455
ZH 时间线只往后加，不回头改：观点的每一次变化，按我们什么时候知道的往后记。晚到的信息，同一件事已经有更新的说法，它就不算数，不加进观点，只在处理记录里写一笔“过时，没用”；讲的是我们不知道的事，照常算，记上它真实的日期。分这两种由模型比证据时一起判，不另加规矩。
EN The timeline only appends, never rewrites past knowledge. A late statement already superseded by a newer one is logged as superseded and unused, not added to the thesis. Previously unknown information counts normally with its true date. The evidence-matching model distinguishes these cases; add no separate rule.
503 ORDER_RULES.6 @456
ZH 一条信息出了修正版，只换它自己那一处出处：修正版只是转述别人的，不动原来那条证据；修正版本身就是原始来源的，改了的原句由新句替代，删了的标“被替代”。连着被改了、被删了的原句的开着的观点各重判一次；只换了转述出处的，不重判；过去的重判记录不改。
EN A revised input changes only its own source reference. Revising a retelling does not change original evidence. For an original-source revision, changed statements are replaced and deleted statements marked replaced. Rejudge each open thesis linked to affected statements once. A retelling-reference change alone does not trigger rejudgement. Keep old judgement records unchanged.
504 ORDER_RULES.7 @457
ZH 失败：每条信息记下做到哪一步，从失败的那一步重试，重试只替换自己上次的结果；多次失败的放进人工复核池。
EN On failure, record the item's completed step and retry from the failed step, replacing only that attempt's own result. Repeated failures go to human review.
505 ORDER_RULES.8 @458
